  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: High Card Pool (Red Dog/Slippery Sam). Banking game. Setup: 3-8 players, 52-card deck, 5 cards dealt per player. Ante to pot. Turn sequence: Player bets (ante to full pot). Dealer burns, draws next card. Win: Have card of same suit and higher rank. Win = take bet + equal from pot. Lose = bet â†’ pot. Card ranks: A(14) K(13) Q(12) J(11) 10-2. Dealer rotates.',
    Player: "Welcome to High Card Pool, the game of probability and nerve. You're dealt 5 cards. You bet against the potâ€”from the ante up to the full amount. Then the dealer draws a card. If you hold a card of the same suit that's higher in rank, you win your bet plus the same amount from the pot. If not, your bet goes in the pot and you lose. Play the odds, manage your bankroll, and watch the pot grow.",
    objective: 'Win the pot by having a card in your hand that is the same suit as and higher in rank than a card dealt from the remaining deck.',
    gameplay: "1. Starting to the left of the dealer, each player makes a bet against the current pot.\n2. **Betting**: You must bet at least the ante and may bet up to the total amount in the pot.\n3. **The Reveal**: Once the bet is placed, the dealer 'burns' one card and then reveals the next card from the deck.\n4. **Outcome**: - If you have a card of the SAME suit and HIGHER rank than the revealed card, you WIN and take your stake + an equal amount from the pot. - If you do NOT have a card of that suit or your cards of that suit are LOWER, you LOSE and your stake is added to the pot.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for High Card Pool.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Players bet against the central pot.',
      'Winning condition: Win the pot by having a card in your hand that is the same suit as and higher in rank than a card dealt from the remaining deck.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '3 to 8 players.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. A (high) to 2 (low).',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. A (high) to 2 (low).',
      dealing: 'The dealer deals 5 cards face down to each player (4 or 3 cards in some variants to accommodate more players).',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Starting to the left of the dealer, each player makes a bet against the current pot.\n2. **Betting**: You must bet at least the ante and may bet up to the total amount in the pot.\n3. **The Reveal**: Once the bet is placed, the dealer 'burns' one card and then reveals the next card from the deck.\n4. **Outcome**: - If you have a card of the SAME suit and HIGHER rank than the revealed card, you WIN and take your stake + an equal amount from the pot. - If you do NOT have a card of that suit or your cards of that suit are LOWER, you LOSE and your stake is added to the pot.",
